### 5.4 Data reliability requirements

Each external data observation must contain:

* Source identifier.

* Retrieval timestamp.

* Geographic resolution.

* Original measurement.

* Unit of measurement.

* Transformation history.

* Freshness indicator.

* Confidence or uncertainty.

* Source licensing and access restrictions.

Public datasets must not be described as real-time unless their actual update frequency supports that claim.

Environmental hazard information must distinguish confirmed incidents, reported incidents, historical records, and model-generated estimates.

### 6\. Community mesh and communication resilience

### 6.1 Transport hierarchy

| Priority   | Transport                  | Operational purpose                 |
| ---------- | -------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Primary    | HTTPS / WebSocket          | Normal messaging                    |
| Secondary  | WebRTC                     | Direct peer communication           |
| Tertiary   | Local Wi-Fi / Wi-Fi Direct | Nearby device exchange              |
| Quaternary | Bluetooth LE               | Discovery and small payloads        |
| Fallback   | SMS                        | Compact emergency signaling         |
| Optional   | Compatible RF hardware     | Specialized emergency communication |

Engineering correction: WebRTC is a peer-communication protocol, not a complete offline mesh architecture. A separate discovery, routing, and store-and-forward layer is required.

Legacy 56k dial-up should be treated as an experimental transport adapter rather than an assumed Android capability.

### 6.2 Store-and-forward

Each mesh node maintains:

* Bounded encrypted message cache.

* Message expiration.

* Duplicate detection.

* Sender authentication.

* Relay permissions.

* Delivery acknowledgment.

* Synchronization history.

### 6.3 Node swap mechanism

```text
ACTIVE NODE
     |
HEALTH MONITOR
     |
+----+----------------+
|                     |
HEALTHY              DEGRADED
|                     |
CONTINUE             SELECT STANDBY
                      |
                 VALIDATE STATE
                      |
                 TRANSFER LEAD
                      |
