### 7.3 Escrow safeguards

The escrow system must support:

* Explicit buyer authorization.

* Explicit seller acceptance.

* Clearly defined transaction terms.

* Asset and payment verification.

* Delivery evidence.

* Dispute submission.

* Human review where necessary.

* Refund and settlement procedures.

An oracle provides external observations; it does not independently guarantee physical delivery or product quality.

Escrow must remain disabled until smart-contract audits, supported wallet integrations, applicable legal review, and dispute procedures are complete.

