### 10.1 GPS RTG

Movement measurements should distinguish:

* Device-reported steps.

* GPS-derived distance.

* Accelerometer estimates.

* Manually entered activity.

* Estimated versus verified measurements.

KL divergence can be used to measure distributional differences between observed and reference data.

For probability distributions and :

D_{KL}(P\\parallel Q)
=
\\sum_i P(i)\\log\\frac{P(i)}{Q(i)}

It is not itself an estimator of squared residual error. Prediction error and residual analysis must be separately defined.

