Participants must control location sharing and personal channel discovery.

### 14\. Market Integrity Leaderboard

### 14.1 Performance metrics

The leaderboard should evaluate market performance independently from personal popularity.

| Metric              | Description                                              |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Highest Price Sold  | Highest verified completed sale                          |
| Lowest Price Bought | Lowest verified purchase                                 |
| Trade-to-Sell Ratio | Completed sales relative to sell offers                  |
| Trade-to-Buy Ratio  | Completed purchases relative to buy requests             |
| Quickest Return     | Shortest verified transaction duration                   |
| Longest Return      | Longest completed transaction duration                   |
| Best Offer          | Best qualifying offer under defined criteria             |
| Volume Uniqueness   | Distinct transaction participation                       |
| Market Sentiment    | Aggregated directional activity                          |
| Fulfillment Rate    | Completed transactions relative to accepted transactions |

### 14.2 Anti-manipulation controls

The system must detect or flag:

* Wash trading.

* Duplicate listings.

* Artificial volume.

* Coordinated false offers.

* Circular transactions.

* Repeated self-dealing.

* Manipulated price signals.

Leaderboard rewards must not be based solely on transaction volume.

### 14.3 Auto Team Returns

Auto Team Returns groups participants according to compatible trade preferences, geographic proximity, fulfillment history, and available inventory.

The matching system must disclose its ranking factors and avoid using sensitive attributes as hidden eligibility criteria.

